Z||000000||Adrift||12-01-2001||05:09 PM||||I pulled out the oil dipstick to check my oil and it won't go back in now, not with the engine running or off. Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-01-2001||06:53 PM||||<BR>Try checking the dipstick tube, make sure it didn't pull out. (Should be obvious if its loose.) Hopefully you didn't lose the screw that holds it in... <P>If not, try twisting dipstick as you put it in. Mine does same thing. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed<BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red & shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||11
Z||000002||SLYGUY||12-01-2001||09:03 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by REDHOTT88:<BR><B><BR>try twisting dipstick as you put it in. Mine does same thing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ditto here. Every car I've ever had is the same. You'd think that metal-oil-metal would not bind, but it does.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly<BR><p>[This message has been edited by SLYGUY (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||1
